<title>GERMANY: German Bunds wobble, then steady after U.S. data.</title>
<headline>German Bunds wobble, then steady after U.S. data.</headline>
<text>
<p>1233 GMT - German Bunds and futures slip with Treasuries then recover after U.S. Q2 employment cost index gains 0.8 pct versus 0.6 pct previous -- bang in line with expectations.</p>
<p>* 6.00% July 2007 Bund 103.50, yld 5.524 pct bid (103.26)</p>
<p>* Sept Bund future 103.11 (102.84),range so far 102.97-103.14</p>
